---
import { SITE } from "@config/constants";

const mail = `mailto:${SITE.email}`;
---

<div>
  <section class="phero" data-hero>
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="label" aria-hidden="true"><i></i>Privacy</span>
      <h1>Privacy</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        This page explains what information Teesside Digital collects through this website, why, who else handles it, and what you can ask Dave to do with it.
      </p>
      <p class="updated">Last updated: 13 October 2026</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <div class="legal">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="prose">
      <section aria-labelledby="responsible-heading">
        <h2 id="responsible-heading">Who is responsible</h2>
        <div>
          <p>
            Teesside Digital is run by David Young as a sole trader. Dave is
            responsible for the personal information described here (the "data
            controller", in data-protection terms).
          </p>
          <p>
            For anything about your information, email
            <a href={mail}>{SITE.email}</a>.
          </p>
          <!-- TODO: add full postal address when a business address service is set up -->
          <p>Based in Hartlepool, Teesside.</p>
          <!-- TODO: retake ICO fee self-assessment once trading; add registration number here if one is issued -->
        </div>
      </section>
      <section aria-labelledby="collected-heading">
        <h2 id="collected-heading">What is collected</h2>
        <div>
          <p>
            <strong>When you send an enquiry</strong>, the form asks for your
            name, email address and a description of what you need, and
            optionally your business name, website address and a budget or
            spending limit.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>When you request a website review</strong>, the form asks for
            your name, email address and the website you want reviewed, and
            optionally anything you would like Dave to look at.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>When you email Dave directly</strong>, he receives whatever
            you include in your message.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>When you visit any page</strong>, the website's host
            automatically processes technical information needed to deliver the
            page and keep the site secure, such as your IP address, browser type
            and the pages requested.
          </p>
          <p>
            Please do not send passwords, payment details or sensitive personal
            information through the forms or by email.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section aria-labelledby="why-heading">
        <h2 id="why-heading">Why it is used</h2>
        <div>
          <ul role="list">
            <li>
              <strong>Enquiries:</strong> to reply to you and discuss the work you
              have described. This is done because you asked for it, and so Dave
              can take the steps needed before any agreement.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Website reviews:</strong> to carry out the review you
              requested and email you the report. This is done because you asked
              for it.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Client records:</strong> if you go on to work with Teesside
              Digital, your details are kept to deliver the work, invoice for it
              and meet tax and accounting obligations.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Technical information:</strong> to deliver the website and
              protect it from misuse.
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Your details are not used for marketing, not added to a mailing list,
            and not sold.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section aria-labelledby="handlers-heading">
        <h2 id="handlers-heading">Who else handles it</h2>
        <div>
          <p>
            Dave uses two services that process your information on his behalf:
          </p>
          <ul role="list">
            <li>
              <strong>Netlify</strong>, which hosts this website and receives form
              submissions. Netlify is based in the United States, so form
              submissions and technical information are processed there.
              <a href="https://www.netlify.com/privacy/"
                >Read Netlify's privacy policy</a
              >
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Zoho Mail</strong>, which provides Dave's email. Messages
              are held in Zoho's EU data centre.
              <a href="https://www.zoho.com/privacy.html"
                >Read Zoho's privacy policy</a
              >
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Netlify protects information transferred outside the UK using the UK
            Extension to the EU-U.S. Data Privacy Framework.
          </p>
          <p>
            Nobody else has access to your information unless the law requires
            it.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section aria-labelledby="kept-heading">
        <h2 id="kept-heading">How long it is kept</h2>
        <div>
          <ul role="list">
            <li>
              <strong>Copies of form submissions held by Netlify:</strong> deleted
              within 30 days. Dave keeps the email copy.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Enquiries that do not lead to work:</strong> deleted 12
              months after the last contact.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Website review requests and reports:</strong> deleted 12
              months after the report is sent.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Client records:</strong> kept for as long as tax law
              requires, which for a sole trader is usually around six years.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Technical information processed by the host:</strong> kept
              according to Netlify's own retention, outside Dave's control.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section aria-labelledby="storage-heading">
        <h2 id="storage-heading">Cookies and storage</h2>
        <div>
          <p>
            This website does not use cookies, analytics or tracking, and does
            not load content from other websites.
          </p>
          <p>
            If you choose Dark or Light using the theme switch, your browser
            remembers that choice on your own device so the site looks the same
            next time. It is not sent anywhere. You can clear it through your
            browser settings.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section aria-labelledby="rights-heading">
        <h2 id="rights-heading">Your rights</h2>
        <div>
          <p>You can ask Dave to:</p>
          <ul role="list">
            <li>
              tell you what information he holds about you, and give you a copy;
            </li>
            <li>correct information that is wrong;</li>
            <li>delete your information;</li>
            <li>stop or limit how it is used;</li>
            <li>
              give you your information in a format you can take elsewhere.
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            To ask, email <a href={mail}>{SITE.email}</a>. Dave will reply within
            one month, as the law requires. You will not be charged.
          </p>
          <p>
            If you are unhappy with how your information has been handled, you
            can complain to the Information Commissioner's Office, the UK
            data-protection regulator.
            <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/"
              >Visit the ICO website</a
            >
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section aria-labelledby="changes-heading">
        <h2 id="changes-heading">Changes to this notice</h2>
        <div>
          <p>
            If the way this website handles information changes, this page will
            be updated and the date at the top will change.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
